// `kinds` names the family first and the semantic kind second: `KeywordAction`
// is the declaration's identity, `Instruction` the position its body occupies,
// so a keyword action resolves where a card writes an instruction.
//
// A declaration file writes its action's instruction (`body`) and never who
// performs it: that is the actor, the controller unless a handoff
// (`act(performer, …)`) names another player or a permanent (ADR 7, rulings
// 2026-10-05). The body here is the record of what the file wrote, and
// `deckmaste_semantics_v2::keywords` builds the action's definition from it:
// `Enact(verb: <deed>, instruction: <body>)`, performed by the actor in
// context, where the deed is `Action(<label>)`, the label the words the name
// spells, unless the file writes `deed`. `deed: None` leaves the instruction
// unwrapped, and a declaration with no body stays bodyless. An action a
// permanent performs (explore, endure, adapt, harness, monstrosity) is
// performed by the actor as well: under a handoff to a permanent the actor is
// that permanent, and with none the source permanent performs it (Lean
// `enactPerformer`, `enactAgentOk`).
(
    name: "KeywordAction",
    kinds: [Macro],
    params: {
        "name": String,
        "params": Elidable(Any),
        "spelling": String,
        "grammar": Elidable(Any),
        "deed": Elidable(Any),
        "body": Default(Any, ()),
    },
    body: (
        name: Param(name),
        kinds: [KeywordAction, Instruction],
        params: Param(params),
        metadata: (
            spelling: Param(spelling),
            grammar: Param(grammar),
        ),
        body: (deed: Param(deed), instruction: Param(body)),
    ),
)
